 thus, matching input  thereafter  must match the  \n  character too. 

 Thus, to  match a newline  inside  a multiline input string , it is better to use the following regexes: 

 '\n'  to match (and consume) a LF alone (a Unix-format newline) 

 '\r\n'  to match (and consume) a CR followed by a LF (a Windows-format newline sequence) 

 '\r?\n'  to match (and consume) a LF  possibly  preceded by a CR, i.e. to match  both  Windows-format and Unix-format newlines. 

